WEBVTT

00:27.650 --> 00:30.670
Love, I've got to feel it

00:30.950 --> 00:34.000
If you put your trust in me

00:34.270 --> 00:37.520
I know what my life would be

00:37.590 --> 00:42.410
Oh, you are all I ever need

00:42.570 --> 00:48.110
I try to hear what you say

00:48.260 --> 00:50.380
So I pray

00:50.460 --> 00:53.960
But you're fading away

00:55.400 --> 01:01.120
Don't go and break my fragile heart

01:01.550 --> 01:04.750
We won't fall apart

01:04.870 --> 01:12.930
'Cause you're my only star

01:14.890 --> 01:18.640
I wonder why my tears come at night

01:18.640 --> 01:22.150
Calling you, so like a little child

01:22.310 --> 01:25.390
All the things you have in mind

01:25.650 --> 01:28.770
I wish I could see your insides

01:28.770 --> 01:31.800
My love, you've got to feel it

01:31.800 --> 01:35.110
And if we put our trust in you and me

01:35.320 --> 01:38.770
You know what our lives would be

01:38.890 --> 01:46.730
Oh, you are the one, I believe

01:58.000 --> 01:59.890
All because!

01:59.890 --> 02:01.050
All because...

02:01.050 --> 02:01.760
All because!

02:03.930 --> 02:04.760
All because...

02:06.390 --> 02:07.180
All because...

02:08.430 --> 02:10.560
All because I let go of those hands!

02:12.940 --> 02:13.880
Yes...

02:15.460 --> 02:18.860
It's all your fault, Yu-kun.

02:26.810 --> 02:30.730
Did I... abandon her?

02:30.730 --> 02:32.490
Did I abandon someone yet again?

02:39.290 --> 02:41.630
If it's something I can obtain,

02:43.130 --> 02:44.300
I'll go get it.

02:45.550 --> 02:47.340
And if it's something I can't obtain...

02:48.830 --> 02:50.720
I won't desire it in the first place.

02:51.190 --> 02:53.100
If it's a battle I can win, then I'll fight.

02:55.100 --> 02:58.850
If it's a battle I know I'll lose, then I'll avoid it from the outset.

02:59.410 --> 03:01.170
Now that I think about it,

03:01.170 --> 03:02.860
I've always done things that way.

03:04.860 --> 03:06.860
I arranged them so neatly, too.

03:07.240 --> 03:09.870
Entropy always increases.

03:11.570 --> 03:15.200
It's meaningless to decrease it in the hope of increasing it.

03:15.400 --> 03:18.080
That's true. I agree with you on that.

03:19.890 --> 03:22.840
It's also meaningless to meet someone when you know that you'll just end up separated.

03:23.380 --> 03:27.840
If I said that, I wonder if being born just to die would be considered meaningless as well.

03:29.340 --> 03:33.930
Kuze, are you really okay about Miki-chan?

03:33.930 --> 03:36.170
Yeah. Of course.

03:36.170 --> 03:37.560
No worries, Nagi.

03:39.950 --> 03:42.690
With this, I feel like I can spend the rest of my life in peace.

03:48.870 --> 03:52.120
I feel like I'm going to have that dream again.

03:52.120 --> 03:54.120
and

04:09.970 --> 04:12.090
What do you want, Senpai?

04:12.360 --> 04:13.510
Are you going back?

04:14.670 --> 04:16.680
Are you going back to Amamiya's place?

04:16.680 --> 04:18.170
Yes.

04:18.170 --> 04:19.690
Because it's my home.

04:22.160 --> 04:23.450
Don't!

04:24.480 --> 04:25.800
Why not?

04:25.800 --> 04:27.800
If you go back, he's going to do it again!

04:27.800 --> 04:32.240
It's the only place I can return to.

04:33.200 --> 04:35.390
I'm not going to let you go back to him!

04:35.390 --> 04:36.660
Please let me go.

04:36.660 --> 04:39.120
Do you really want to go back?

04:39.320 --> 04:40.750
Do you want to go on enduring it?!

04:43.250 --> 04:45.040
Why are you concerned <i>now?</i>

04:48.460 --> 04:50.470
Believe

05:01.290 --> 05:04.810
Is weeding your new hobby now, Yu?

05:05.370 --> 05:06.520
Nagi...

05:08.760 --> 05:10.010
I heard about it.

05:10.010 --> 05:12.890
When in the world did you become Kuze's fiancée?

05:12.890 --> 05:16.140
I just thought that something like that would be for the best.

05:16.140 --> 05:19.030
A lie that could be discovered so easily?

05:19.030 --> 05:20.630
That's not important.

05:20.630 --> 05:21.660
It got results.

05:22.730 --> 05:26.860
As long as Miki-chan knows that Kuze wants to distance himself from her,

05:26.860 --> 05:28.920
the words used on the surface don't matter.

05:29.420 --> 05:32.030
They're not important if she can see through his mask.

05:32.030 --> 05:34.300
What's hidden inside is his true nature.

05:34.730 --> 05:37.930
Does he need to continue concealing his true nature?

05:37.930 --> 05:41.310
When we were still in school, Kuze had feelings for me.

05:42.180 --> 05:43.560
You didn't know?

05:43.560 --> 05:44.750
No...

05:44.750 --> 05:45.960
That's news to me.

05:45.960 --> 05:49.550
He knew that I had feelings for you.

05:49.550 --> 05:52.090
That's why he chose to keep quiet.

05:52.090 --> 05:53.390
I see.

05:53.390 --> 05:57.150
I never expected a womanizer like him to value friendship more. It must be his morals.

05:57.150 --> 05:58.830
That's not it.

05:58.830 --> 06:01.370
It's just that he won't enter a competition he can't win.

06:02.690 --> 06:06.230
Oh, wow. I was like that back then.

06:06.230 --> 06:07.570
Nagi...

06:07.570 --> 06:11.070
Yu, are you also still hanging on to a competition from the past?

06:11.070 --> 06:13.890
Who knows? I've already forgotten.

06:13.890 --> 06:15.440
You look back a lot, don't you?

06:15.440 --> 06:18.000
I've got eyes in the back of my head too, that's all.

06:18.000 --> 06:18.760
And also...

06:20.060 --> 06:22.890
I don't feel like the competition has ended.

06:22.890 --> 06:24.890
Touch

06:24.890 --> 06:27.880
Why did you decide to tell me everything about it <i>now?</i>

06:27.880 --> 06:29.310
What are you talking about?

06:29.730 --> 06:32.050
Why didn't you tell me earlier?

06:32.050 --> 06:34.890
You really say some unreasonable things.

06:34.890 --> 06:38.140
Would it have made a difference if I'd told you earlier?

06:38.140 --> 06:41.310
Would you have done anything for me if I had?

06:41.310 --> 06:42.600
If I'd told you earlier...

06:42.770 --> 06:44.080
If I'd told you earlier...

06:44.470 --> 06:48.290
would you have come to love damaged goods like me?

06:48.960 --> 06:50.530
That's...!

06:50.530 --> 06:52.570
You're a cruel person.

06:52.570 --> 06:54.130
This is revenge.

06:55.130 --> 06:59.640
It's a small revenge against you for abandoning me.

07:01.140 --> 07:04.460
But it's only natural, right?

07:04.460 --> 07:08.550
Even when you were at the orphanage, you lived by yourself,

07:08.550 --> 07:11.010
despite being caught in an abyss of misfortune.

07:11.010 --> 07:15.970
You did everything by yourself, from the beginning to the end.

07:15.970 --> 07:20.160
That's why there was no room for an outsider like me.

07:20.520 --> 07:26.650
I wanted you to have a taste of my pain, even if only a little bit.

07:26.650 --> 07:30.070
That's why I approached you.

07:30.070 --> 07:33.000
I tried to make you fall in love with me.

07:33.180 --> 07:35.800
I cut my own shoes with this.

07:36.970 --> 07:39.340
Then... about the bullying...

07:39.760 --> 07:42.350
I really <i>was being bullied.</i>

07:42.350 --> 07:44.160
I used it to my advantage,

07:44.160 --> 07:48.440
because I thought it would greatly appeal to your strong sense of justice.

07:48.870 --> 07:51.190
"If you despise me, you can kill me."

07:52.130 --> 07:56.470
My brother said that and gave this to me...

07:56.470 --> 07:58.610
on that Christmas night.

07:59.120 --> 08:00.930
You know, this is my protective charm.

08:00.930 --> 08:06.020
Because as long as I have it, I can be free whenever I want.

08:06.020 --> 08:08.660
That is the one and only thing that has kept me going.

08:20.380 --> 08:22.390
The

08:22.390 --> 08:25.210
Please tell me about Kuze-san.

08:25.210 --> 08:26.500
You should ask him yourself.

08:26.500 --> 08:28.890
If I could, I wouldn't be so concerned!

08:28.890 --> 08:32.520
You could only call this an effort if you did your best and actually solved the problem.

08:32.790 --> 08:35.160
I thought about making an effort,

08:35.160 --> 08:38.550
and I concluded that coming to ask you would be the fastest way.

08:38.550 --> 08:41.940
You confessed your love and were rejected right away, huh?

08:43.100 --> 08:46.230
You were lucky that you only went through a small amount of pain.

08:46.230 --> 08:47.600
He's an adult.

08:47.600 --> 08:49.620
I'm not a child either!

08:51.180 --> 08:54.610
Problems certainly arise when both of you look forward, don't they?

08:54.610 --> 08:58.000
I think that the current Kuze-san looks backward a lot.

08:58.480 --> 09:00.880
He also has eyes in the back of his head.

09:02.090 --> 09:06.710
If you really want to confront Kuze, remember one thing.

09:06.710 --> 09:09.750
You can rely on him, but don't take his word for anything.

09:09.750 --> 09:11.040
How come?

09:11.040 --> 09:12.750
Because he's a liar.

09:12.750 --> 09:13.770
A liar?

09:14.210 --> 09:15.900
Just remember that.

09:21.100 --> 09:24.820
Kuze-san is not a liar.

09:25.230 --> 09:29.700
If he really was, wouldn't it have been easier for him to say that he hated me?

09:30.090 --> 09:33.960
Because he's so honest, his lies are easy to detect.

09:35.630 --> 09:37.630
Follow

09:37.630 --> 09:39.510
Onii-chan

09:37.630 --> 09:39.510
Six months ago Kuza-san was
stricken by a heart attack during
a concert. After that, he retired
from musical activities. Since then,
he has been recovering at his home
in Australia. no other information
has been released to the public.

09:37.980 --> 09:40.710
Apparently, no other information has been released to the public.

09:40.710 --> 09:42.240
I see.

09:42.240 --> 09:45.830
When I told him the story about Kuze-san, onii-chan was shocked as well.

09:45.830 --> 09:48.710
Does Hiro-senpai know Kuze-san too?

09:48.710 --> 09:51.380
Onii-chan is a fan of Kuze Shuichi.

09:51.380 --> 09:54.350
When he draws, he always listens to Kuze's albums!

09:54.350 --> 09:56.050
Is that so?

09:56.050 --> 09:59.720
He says that he can see colors within the sounds of Kuze-san's violin.

09:59.720 --> 10:00.360
Colors?

10:00.360 --> 10:07.180
Yeah. He said that it feels like every color in the world is held inside.

10:07.180 --> 10:09.940
Although I don't know exactly what he means by that.

10:09.940 --> 10:12.440
I understand.

10:12.440 --> 10:13.120
Huh?

10:13.120 --> 10:21.320
The tone that Kuze-san plays is so vivid, so deep, and so clear.

10:21.320 --> 10:25.510
But the last time I heard it, not all the colors were there.

10:26.870 --> 10:30.220
I felt... as if some colors were missing.

10:31.040 --> 10:32.600
Wait a moment!

10:32.600 --> 10:32.970
Mail

10:32.600 --> 10:32.970
Internet

10:32.600 --> 10:32.970
Camera

10:32.600 --> 10:32.970
iApps

10:32.600 --> 10:32.970
Data

10:32.600 --> 10:32.970
Tools

10:32.970 --> 10:33.600
Email
Menu

10:32.970 --> 10:33.600
Compose
New
Message

10:32.970 --> 10:33.600
Inbox

10:32.970 --> 10:33.600
Sent

10:32.970 --> 10:33.600
Search

10:37.200 --> 10:40.340
He said that perhaps Kuze-san is uncertain about something.

10:40.340 --> 10:43.630
"Although it's probably different for each person, if you're uncertain,

10:43.630 --> 10:46.740
adding certain colors may not be possible."

10:46.740 --> 10:50.990
He suggested that perhaps you can't color the parts where there's uncertainty.

10:50.990 --> 10:54.310
Hiro-senpai sure talks big.

10:54.310 --> 10:56.370
That was Miyamura-senpai.

10:56.370 --> 11:05.130
On phone: From Miyamura-senpai. Perhaps he's uncertain about something? Although it's probably different for each person, if you're not uncertain, you should be able to add some kind of color. Maybe it's not possible to color parts where there is uncertainty...?

10:56.840 --> 11:01.450
Both Miyamura-senpai and onii-chan were looking for the colors they lacked.

11:01.450 --> 11:05.130
Maybe I was the same way.

11:05.130 --> 11:07.950
I don't know all the complexities,

11:07.950 --> 11:11.780
but I'm sure that everyone becomes a little uncertain...

11:11.780 --> 11:13.390
when they find out they're going to die.

11:13.750 --> 11:17.700
If anything, I think his uncertainty is causing him to try and throw things away.

11:17.700 --> 11:18.920
All sorts of things.

11:18.920 --> 11:20.770
Throwing things away because he's uncertain?

11:21.040 --> 11:24.030
Aren't some things painful if you treasure them deeply?

11:28.030 --> 11:31.530
If the darkness cuts the memory

11:28.030 --> 11:31.530
And it still doesn't stop

11:48.170 --> 11:49.340
What is it...

11:51.260 --> 11:52.720
Himura-kun?

11:55.760 --> 11:58.350
I see. So it's about Yuko.

11:58.350 --> 11:59.100
Yeah.

11:59.100 --> 12:02.020
Oh, you <i>just heard about it?</i>

12:02.020 --> 12:06.480
It's not like I prevented her from telling anyone,
so she should've just talked to you.

12:06.690 --> 12:07.490
Hey!

12:08.530 --> 12:10.360
What the hell are you saying?

12:10.360 --> 12:12.620
Do you have any idea what you've done?!

12:14.330 --> 12:19.360
Could it be... that you're here to kill me?

12:19.360 --> 12:21.710
Then that's fine. Go ahead and kill me.

12:22.540 --> 12:25.860
Just kill me. I'll be grateful.

12:25.860 --> 12:28.750
But what do you plan on doing after that?

12:28.750 --> 12:31.200
You're aiming for the top rung, aren't you?

12:31.200 --> 12:35.050
Are you going to throw away your status as a scholarship student?

12:35.050 --> 12:36.710
Just kidding.

12:36.710 --> 12:41.190
You're not one to put a trifling matter like that on the same scale as this.

12:41.190 --> 12:43.900
Did Yuko tell you to kill me?

12:43.900 --> 12:46.020
Yuko would never say something like that.

12:46.020 --> 12:49.360
Well then, <i>you're the one who wants to kill me, correct?</i>

12:49.360 --> 12:50.360
That's not true!

12:50.760 --> 12:54.370
Surely, you're not going to say that it's for Yuko, are you?

12:55.580 --> 12:58.650
My, my. You're truly a child.

12:58.650 --> 12:59.860
What?!

12:59.860 --> 13:03.330
Can you... see the colors?

13:09.070 --> 13:14.050
Your assumptions are going to bring Yuko misfortune again.

13:14.050 --> 13:18.290
Yuko has been afraid of being alone...

13:18.290 --> 13:22.460
ever since you rejected her when she was young.

13:22.460 --> 13:26.360
Why are you trying to take away Yuko's home?

13:26.360 --> 13:28.920
A place like this isn't Yuko's home!

13:28.920 --> 13:30.430
I see.

13:30.430 --> 13:33.600
Well, since you reached that conclusion after much thought,

13:33.600 --> 13:35.070
do as you like.

13:36.570 --> 13:42.830
Why do you think Yuko never went to the police or the school or anyone else?

13:43.590 --> 13:45.790
She's a girl, after all.

13:45.790 --> 13:49.050
She couldn't possibly tell a stranger about something like this, could she?

13:51.300 --> 13:54.080
If I were to die, all of it would leak out.

13:54.080 --> 13:56.160
Every last bit.

13:56.160 --> 14:03.390
Basically, you're going to reveal Yuko's disgrace and shame her, for your own selfish reasons.

14:03.390 --> 14:04.500
What's wrong?

14:04.500 --> 14:05.640
Aren't you going to do it?

14:06.300 --> 14:09.270
Aren't you going to kill me?

14:09.270 --> 14:11.230
That's the reason you came here, isn't it?

14:14.710 --> 14:15.360
Now...

14:34.090 --> 14:37.840
You came here without the courage to kill?!

14:38.720 --> 14:43.130
You brat, you only have a vision of courage, but you're incapable of acting!

14:44.980 --> 14:46.770
If you're serious, why can't you do it?!

14:46.770 --> 14:48.440
Don't hesitate!

14:48.440 --> 14:49.940
Hate me from the depths of your heart!

14:50.940 --> 14:53.090
Hate with all your might!

14:53.090 --> 14:55.150
If you're serious, why can't you do it?!

14:59.500 --> 15:01.350
I told you.

15:01.350 --> 15:06.210
If you want to make Yuko yours, then prepare yourself.

15:06.210 --> 15:09.740
Next time you come, be really prepared.

15:09.740 --> 15:13.800
If not, I'll kill you.

15:23.310 --> 15:25.310
Form

15:31.270 --> 15:32.930
Yo, Nagi.

15:32.930 --> 15:34.650
Did you buy some cigarettes for me?

15:35.430 --> 15:36.530
Good evening!

15:38.320 --> 15:39.740
Kuze-san?

15:40.100 --> 15:44.560
A certain violinist was hiking in the mountains.

15:44.560 --> 15:48.860
It was a path that he knew well, but perhaps due to carelessness,

15:48.860 --> 15:51.880
he slipped and fell off the cliff.

15:52.880 --> 15:57.200
And in order to protect his hands, which are a performer's life,

15:57.200 --> 16:00.130
he hit his head on a boulder and died.

16:03.560 --> 16:06.790
I told you never to come see me again, didn't I?

16:06.790 --> 16:09.420
Umm, I wanted to talk to you about something!

16:09.420 --> 16:10.900
I have nothing to say to you.

16:10.900 --> 16:14.260
Well then, would you like to go out for some soft-serve ice cream?

16:14.260 --> 16:15.650
My treat.

16:15.880 --> 16:17.400
Would you please disappear?

16:21.660 --> 16:23.300
What should I do?

16:23.300 --> 16:24.660
"Do?" What do you mean?

16:24.660 --> 16:28.910
I definitely don't want us... to part like this.

16:31.420 --> 16:33.920
Mizuki-chan, do you love me?

16:33.920 --> 16:35.030
Yes.

16:35.030 --> 16:36.790
Do you <i>really love me?</i>

16:36.790 --> 16:37.420
Yes!

16:37.420 --> 16:38.490
Why?

16:38.490 --> 16:39.720
"Why?" I—

16:39.720 --> 16:42.370
Why are you standing there?

16:42.370 --> 16:45.180
Why are you standing there shamelessly like that?

16:45.570 --> 16:47.810
Why are you looking at my eyes?

16:47.810 --> 16:50.810
Why are you listening to my voice?

16:50.810 --> 16:53.310
Why are you in front of me?

16:53.310 --> 16:55.810
Why are you speaking to me?

16:55.810 --> 16:58.320
Why are you following me around?

16:58.320 --> 17:01.070
Why are you trying to care for me?

17:01.070 --> 17:03.610
Why won't you leave me alone?

17:03.610 --> 17:05.820
Why did you meet me?

17:06.000 --> 17:08.450
Why did you get to know me?

17:08.560 --> 17:11.080
Why did you appear in front of me?

17:11.390 --> 17:13.080
Why did you become attached to me?

17:13.370 --> 17:15.210
Why are you smiling?

17:15.450 --> 17:17.460
Why are you meddling?

17:17.670 --> 17:19.590
Why are you in a good mood?

17:19.840 --> 17:21.590
Why are you so happy?

17:21.800 --> 17:23.590
Why aren't you crying?

17:23.800 --> 17:25.590
Why are you cheerful?

17:25.910 --> 17:27.850
Why are you always so pleasant?

17:28.150 --> 17:30.220
Why do you always watch everything?

17:30.470 --> 17:32.730
Why do you always know everything?

17:32.970 --> 17:35.100
Why do you always forgive everything?

17:35.320 --> 17:37.610
Why are you pleased with everything?

17:37.900 --> 17:40.110
Why do you distress me?

17:40.390 --> 17:42.610
Why do you move me?

17:42.650 --> 17:45.110
Why do you baffle me?

17:45.150 --> 17:47.620
Why do you hurt me?

17:47.660 --> 17:50.120
Why do you make me suffer?

17:50.160 --> 17:52.370
Why do you attack me?

17:52.370 --> 17:54.750
Why do you bully me?

17:54.750 --> 17:57.250
Why do you step on me?

17:57.250 --> 17:59.880
Why do you beat me up?

17:59.880 --> 18:02.130
Why do you crush me?

18:02.130 --> 18:04.510
Why do you tear me apart?

18:04.510 --> 18:07.140
Why do you pound me?

18:07.140 --> 18:09.510
Why won't you forgive me?

18:09.510 --> 18:12.140
Why won't you understand me?

18:12.400 --> 18:14.270
Why do you make me cry?

18:14.490 --> 18:16.650
Why do you give me hope?

18:16.920 --> 18:19.270
Why do you make me despair?

18:19.270 --> 18:21.400
Why do you force me?

18:21.400 --> 18:23.650
Why do you bind me?

18:23.650 --> 18:26.030
Why do you disturb my heart?

18:26.030 --> 18:26.910
Why?

18:26.910 --> 18:28.320
Why? Why?

18:28.320 --> 18:29.240
Why?!

18:31.080 --> 18:32.810
Why do you try to answer?

18:32.810 --> 18:33.750
Because...!

18:34.070 --> 18:35.750
Why do you act familiarly?

18:36.030 --> 18:37.750
Why haven't you gone home yet?

18:37.750 --> 18:39.790
Why are you still there?

18:40.420 --> 18:41.500
Why...

18:43.610 --> 18:45.260
do you exist?

18:55.680 --> 18:57.270
Why is it...

18:57.270 --> 18:59.240
Why...

18:59.240 --> 19:00.520
do you do something like this?

19:01.360 --> 19:03.050
Why...

19:03.050 --> 19:04.530
do you do something so useless?

19:05.370 --> 19:06.910
Why...

19:06.910 --> 19:08.530
do you do something so stupid?

19:12.050 --> 19:13.200
Why...

20:26.230 --> 20:27.640
I can't...

20:27.640 --> 20:29.930
I can't die yet!

20:34.110 --> 20:37.620
How could I... die like this?!

20:38.180 --> 20:41.150
There are still a lot of things I want to do.

20:41.150 --> 20:44.780
A lot that I want to see... A lot that I want to hear!

20:44.780 --> 20:46.040
I don't want to die!

20:46.480 --> 20:50.130
Even music... and the violin... I still...!

20:51.200 --> 20:53.250
Damn it!

20:53.250 --> 20:56.090
I'm going to live, even if it kills me!

20:56.090 --> 20:57.010
Live!

20:59.220 --> 21:00.500
Not yet!

21:00.500 --> 21:01.840
I want to live.

21:01.840 --> 21:04.730
Not yet!

21:09.440 --> 21:12.490
I don't want to goddamn die!

21:28.430 --> 21:41.820
The shining wind calmly sways from gaps in the clouds.

21:42.400 --> 21:49.240
The echoing sounds sparkle.

21:49.370 --> 21:52.740
Even if it's a hope that was nearly lost,

21:52.990 --> 22:00.380
I should be able to find it again

22:02.670 --> 22:05.550
Holding firmly onto your sound,

22:06.170 --> 22:15.730
I don't let go of your hand joined with mine.

22:16.690 --> 22:22.520
Please don't forget the important things.

22:23.690 --> 22:30.200
A smile continues on into the future.

22:48.510 --> 22:49.840
Welcome home, Yuko.

22:49.840 --> 22:51.760
I'm home.

22:51.760 --> 22:54.220
You're going to catch a cold. Hurry up and change.

22:54.220 --> 22:56.770
Yes, onii-san.

23:10.200 --> 23:11.570
Why...

23:14.830 --> 23:16.240
are you doing this <i>now<i>?</i></i>

23:29.300 --> 23:33.680
Throwing everything away, and liquidating everything.

23:33.970 --> 23:36.890
ef - a tale of melodies.

23:37.140 --> 23:38.520
Reutter.

23:39.180 --> 23:42.480
Can you hear it? The melody of truth.
